course: dictionary
lesson: 8259
title: The richness of words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Richness is a noun, something you can have more or less of. When something has richness, it is full of good things: rich colour, rich sound, rich taste or lots of detail. «On the way back the flowers seem to have less of richness and blaze of colour than they seemed to remember seeing quite recently somewhere.» The flowers have less colour and glow than the children remember, so richness means how full of colour something is.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The sentence says less of richness and blaze of colour, so richness goes with colour, and blaze means a bright glow. Test your meaning: "less of being full of colour" makes sense in the sentence, so you have it right.
explain: Richness has other meanings too. Farmers talk about the richness of soil, which means soil full of goodness that helps plants grow. A cake with lots of butter and sugar has a rich taste, which is richness in food.
fact: Richness is a noun. It means being full of something good.
fact: Richness can describe colour, sound, taste or detail.
fact: The richness of soil means it is full of goodness that helps crops grow.
fact: Species richness means how many kinds of living things live in one place.
fact: Richness can mean wealth, but this is rare. Most people say «wealth» instead.
exercise: «On the way back the flowers seem to have less of richness and blaze of colour.» What does richness mean here? | Being very heavy | Being very cold | Being in a hurry | *Being full of colour and glow
exercise: Farmers say the richness of the soil helps crops grow. What does richness mean? | Very hard and dry | *Full of goodness for growing | Being wealthy | Full of stones
exercise: Which word describes a cake full of butter and sugar? | cold | light | *rich | thin
test: Which word do most people use for being wealthy? | *wealth | soil | sound | colour
test: In «rich colour», what does rich mean? | Covered in dust | *Full of bright, lovely colour | Very dark and heavy | Cold and grey
exam: Which sentence uses richness correctly? | The bus was richness | The richness ran up the hill | *The soil has great richness, full of goodness for plants | I had richness for breakfast today
